From 3f5006038b7c83f1e4ac22d4dcb10b4b295a89c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WWE13 Recomp <wwe13-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:30:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] apple: first native macOS build fixes (Xcode 27, Apple
 silicon)

Build fixes found by building on a Mac (Xcode 27.2, macOS 27, arm64).
Linux and Windows behaviour is unchanged.

Linking: FFmpeg shared libraries export av* (and ff_reverse) through
ld64's -exported_symbols_list instead of GNU --version-script. unit_tests
and rex_smoke link rexsystem directly on Apple, because CMake has no
$<LINK_GROUP:RESCAN> for ld64 (and ld64 needs no archive rescans).

libc++: Apple's libc++ has neither std::move_only_function nor
std::chrono::clock_cast. Add rex::move_only_function (an alias of the
std type where the library has it, otherwise a minimal type-erased
replacement) and rex::chrono::clock_time_conversion / clock_cast for
ReXGlue's own clocks, and use them on every platform.

Darwin code that 0104 missed:
- memory_posix: the mach_vm_region helpers were nested inside
  #if REX_PLATFORM_LINUX and never compiled; Protect also reports the old
  access on Darwin. page_size uses sysconf (getpagesize is hidden by
  _XOPEN_SOURCE).
- filesystem_posix, mapped_memory_posix: map the *64 file functions to
  the plain ones (off_t and struct stat are always 64-bit on Darwin).
- dynlib: macOS library names; the Vulkan loader is also tried next to
  the executable, in an app bundle's Frameworks and in the Homebrew and
  /usr/local prefixes.
- renderdoc_app.h: Apple calling convention (as upstream RenderDoc).
- xam_net: socket headers on every POSIX platform, plus <sys/select.h>.
- xsocket: Darwin defines IPPROTO_UDP as a numeric macro, which broke the
  qualified enum name.
- sha256: <machine/endian.h> on Apple.
- heap, disruptorplus: explicit std::min/max types (size_t and uint64_t
  are different types on Darwin).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
